  "articleBody": "When tackling interior home repairs, it’s easy to make a few missteps that can actually make the problem worse or lead to a quick re-do. One common mistake is painting over moisture damage without addressing the source. That fresh paint might look good for a week, but if there's still a leak or condensation issue, the problem will just resurface, sometimes even worse! Always find and fix the underlying cause first. Another pitfall is fixing only the surface when there's hidden damage like rot or mold. It’s like putting a band-aid on a broken arm; it doesn't solve the real issue. You really need to inspect and properly remedy the core problem. People also often underestimate the prep work involved. Skipping proper sanding, priming, or protection of surrounding areas can lead to a messy, unprofessional finish. Lastly, underestimating the time and effort for debris cleanup is a common oversight. Interior projects, especially with drywall or demolition, can create a surprising amount of mess. HH Remodeling LLC always emphasizes proper cleanup and communication throughout the process, which helps avoid these headaches. For more complex repairs, or if you suspect hidden issues, don't hesitate to bring in a professional to ensure the job is done right.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
